  "market_context": "High-volume, high-volatility London/NY session overlap; price exhibited clear uptrend structure with higher highs and higher lows, followed by a strong impulse move breaking prior structure.",
  "key_observation": "After a break of structure (BOS), the analyst drew Fibonacci retracement from the higher low to the higher high of the impulse move and emphasized the 0.618 level as the optimal entry zone (gold zone), even though the price retraced only to 0.5 and missed the limit order.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified an established uptrend via higher highs and higher lows on the 1-minute chart.",
    "Step 2: Recognized an impulse move that broke the previous structure (BOS), confirming trend continuation potential.",
    "Step 3: Drew Fibonacci retracement from the bottom (higher low) to the top (higher high) of that impulse move.",
    "Step 4: Waited for price to retrace into the Fibonacci gold zone (0.5–0.618), noting that the 0.618 level offers the best risk-to-reward for long entries.",
    "Step 5: Set take-profit at the previous swing high and stop-loss below the 1.0 Fibonacci level, acknowledging the entry was missed when price only retraced to 0.5."
  ],
  "outcome": "Entry missed (price retraced only to 0.5, not 0.618); analyst stated the setup remained valid and safest trade would target previous high.",
  "lessons": "In uptrends, the highest-probability Fibonacci entry is at 0.618 (gold zone), not 0.5, despite occasional shallow retracements; always align TP with prior structure and SL below 1.0 Fib for optimal R:R.",
